Description: Fix CVE-2026-58055: nghttpx CONNECT and HTTP Upgrade request smuggling
 nghttpx's HTTP/1.1 handling forwards Upgrade requests that also carry a
 Content-Length header/body onto reusable keep-alive backend connections,
 re-adding the Upgrade and Connection headers while passing Content-Length
 verbatim. A backend that resolves the resulting ambiguous message in the
 attacker's favor enables HTTP request/response smuggling and cross-client
 response-queue poisoning.
 .
 This backport of upstream commit ab28105 tightens CONNECT and HTTP Upgrade
 handling in nghttpx: reject Upgrade/CONNECT requests that carry a body
 (Content-Length or Transfer-Encoding), block forwarding the request body
 until the upgrade is confirmed by the backend, refuse to reuse the backend
 connection while a blocked request buffer is pending, and coerce a 2xx
 response to a CONNECT request that did not upgrade into a 502.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/nghttp2/nghttp2/commit/ab28105c4a0197da24f8bfc414bc116055249e1e
Author: Tatsuhiro Tsujikawa <tatsuhiro.t@gmail.com>
Bug: https://github.com/nghttp2/nghttp2/security/advisories/GHSA-xrr7-82jr-v58x
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/1140917
Last-Update: 2026-07-03

